    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="76">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 76</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>And<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.20"/> gyf hwylc man forstolen þingc ham to his cotan bringe ⁊ he arasod wurðe, riht is, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hæbbe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he æft<hi rend="italic">er</hi>eode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>Be forstolene æhta. Gyf hwa forstolen ðingc ham to his coton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.6"/> bringe ⁊ he arefned<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.7"/> wyrðe, riht his<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.4"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hæbbe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he æft<hi rend="italic">er</hi>eode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="76" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="362" ed="#liebermann"/>And gif hwilc man forstolen þingc ham to his cotan bringe ⁊ he arasod wurðe, riht is, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he habbe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he æftereode.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Si homo furtiuum aliquid in domo sua occultabit et ita<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.13-2"/> fuerit arased<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.14-2"/> (abarnatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.15"/>), rectum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.16"/> est, ut habeat quod quesiuit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis aliquid furtiuum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_76.lnote.oe.13-3"/> ad domum suam portet, et patefactum fuerit, iustum est, ut habeat quod quesiuit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="76" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>[76] Si quis autem furtum in domum suam afferat, et ibi deprehensum fuerit, ipse autem conuictus fuerit, rectum est, ut accipiat hoc quod appetiit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="76" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="212" ed="#robertson"/>Be forstolene æhta. Gyf hwa<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#IICn_76.robnote.fn.12"/> forstolen ðingc ham to his coton bringe ⁊ he arefned<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IICn_76.robnote.fn.13"/> wyrðe, riht is<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#IICn_76.robnote.fn.7"/> þæt he hæbbe þæt he æftereode.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="294" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwylc man forstolen þingc ham to his cotan bringe and he arasod wurðe, riht is þæt he hæbbe þæt he æftereode.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="363" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von gestohlener Fahrhabe. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76.lnote.de.1"/> jemand eine gestohlene Sache heim in seine Hütte bringt und er wird ertappt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76.lnote.de.2"/>, so ist Recht, dass der [Eigenthümer<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_76.lnote.de.3"/>] das erhalte, dem er [spürend] nachging.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of stolen goods. B) And if anyone brings a stolen thing home to his cottage and he is caught, it is right that [the owner] should have what he [tracking] went after.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="213" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning stolen goods. If anyone carries stolen goods home to his cottage and is detected<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#IICn_76.robnote.n.2"/>, the law is that he (the owner) shall have what he has tracked.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_76.whinote.n.1"/><pb n="473" ed="#whitelock"/>And if any man brings home stolen property to his cottage, and he is found out, it is right that he [the owner] should have what he has tracked.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="295" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone brings stolen goods back to his home and is discovered, the law is that the finder shall have that which he has found.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="363"><ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Ine 57?</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="359"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 76-76:1b: Ine 57</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#whitelock" n="473"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref> <quote>With this and the next clauses, cf. Ine 57</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="367"><label>likely reference to</label> <ref target="clause:Ine_57">Ine 57</ref> <quote>Likely references include [...] §76–76.1 (Ine §61)</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares (with a query) Ine 57.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 363, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be forstolene æhta</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">hwylc: hwa B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">arasod: arefned B</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">f. d. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">f. d. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sit <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sit Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">accipiat quod meruit, id est <hi rend="spaced">dignam mortem</hi> <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">accipiat quod meruit, id est <hi rend="italic">dignam mortem</hi> Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. VIII Atr.</hi> 17</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. VIII Atr. 17</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> arefsed?</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read arefsed?</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">f. i. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">f. i. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ar. <hi rend="italic">nur R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ar. only R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">abannitus <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur Hk</hi>; <hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">abannitus on an erasure Hk; lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">r. e. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">r. e. lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">362</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gif hwilce m. f. ðinge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Gif hwilce m. f. ðinge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.oe.13-3" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">363</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">furtum <hi rend="italic">Lb S</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">furtum Lb S</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Spurfolge 3</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Spurfolge 3</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">arasian</hi> ‘als schuldig entdecken’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>.—Dagegen <hi rend="italic">arefned</hi> in B erklärt sich aus anderem Stamme, vielleicht aus <hi rend="italic">æræfe</hi> ‘entdeckt’, <hi rend="italic">aræfan</hi> ‘enthüllen’ <hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi>; im Sinne passt nicht <hi rend="italic">aræfnan</hi> ‘ertragen, ersinnen, ausführen’.—Meine Emendation B's stützt sich auf <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. Af 32².—Q hat <hi rend="italic">abarnare</hi> öfter; <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">arasian</hi> ‘discover to be guilty’; Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl</hi>.—<hi rend="italic">arefned</hi> in B, on the other hand, is to be explained from another stem, perhaps from <hi rend="italic">æræfe</hi> ‘discovered’, <hi rend="italic">aræfan</hi> ‘reveal’ <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi>; <hi rend="italic">aræfnan</hi> ‘endure, devise, carry out’ does not fit the sense.—My emendation of B rests on <hi rend="italic">above</hi> Af 32².—Q frequently has <hi rend="italic">abarnare</hi>; <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_76.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">213</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">C's Glossator * in Hk missversteht, der Dieb erhalte Verdientes, nämlich Todesstrafe des Handhaften; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3. a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">C's glossator * in Hk misunderstands it as meaning that the thief receives his deserts, namely the death penalty of one caught in the act; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3. a</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_76.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. In. 57.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_76.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">I cannot understand <hi rend="italic">arefned</hi>, the reading of B. Liebermann suggests that it is a mistake for <hi rend="italic">arefsed</hi>.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76.robnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope></bibl><label>is</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">his</hi> B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_76.robnote.fn.12" n="12" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope></bibl><label>hwa</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hwylc (hwilc) man</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
